  "name": "nom",
  "description": "Network Object Mirroring (NOM) is a lightweight Python framework for transparent distributed object systems, enabling seamless access and mutation of remote objects across network boundaries. It implements a custom binary serialization protocol over UDP transport, utilizing dynamic proxies to intercept and forward Python magic methods to remote references. The system supports bidirectional communication, remote callbacks, and extensible security through an authentication interface for attribute-level access control.",
